    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A sealed box on the end of a stick. Do not open the box. Inside is, allegedly, a probability core and, allegedly, a cat, and the staff's whole function is to refuse to tell you which until the swing lands. Hits with the confidence of something that already knows how this ends.</p>\n<!-- BBTTCC:MECHANICS:START -->\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>⚙️ Mechanical Effects</strong></p>\n<p>On a hit, roll the 1d12 twice — the wielder chooses which result the universe collapses to (cat alive / cat extremely not). Observers describe the noise differently afterward and are always certain they're right.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d12 Psychic damage to <em>Stress</em> <span style=\"opacity:.75\">(the hit you don't know the size of until it's over)</span></li>\n  <li><strong>Faculty:</strong> Presence</li>\n  <li><strong>Attack:</strong> Channel (Presence)</li>\n  <li><strong>Range:</strong> 5</li>\n  <li><strong>Duration:</strong> Scene</li>\n  <li><strong>Tier:</strong> T1</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- BBTTCC:MECHANICS:END -->"
